198
00:07:20,937 --> 00:07:23,585
Problem number three is invisible from the

199
00:07:23,585 --> 00:07:24,467
driver's seat.

200
00:07:24,816 --> 00:07:27,487
Problem number three is the trailer connection.

201
00:07:27,667 --> 00:07:28,491
Not the hitch.

202
00:07:28,671 --> 00:07:29,913
The electronics.

203
00:07:30,093 --> 00:07:31,852
On February twentieth,

204
00:07:31,852 --> 00:07:35,528
twenty twenty-six, Ford recalled four million,

205
00:07:35,528 --> 00:07:38,245
three hundred eighty-one thousand,

206
00:07:38,245 --> 00:07:41,203
eight hundred seventy-eight vehicles,

207
00:07:41,203 --> 00:07:42,801
including the F-150,

208
00:07:42,801 --> 00:07:45,359
Super Duty, Maverick and Ranger,

209
00:07:45,359 --> 00:07:49,115
because the truck could lose communication with

210
00:07:49,115 --> 00:07:50,074
the trailer.

211
00:07:50,254 --> 00:07:53,192
The trailer's brake lights and turn signals

212
00:07:53,192 --> 00:07:56,402
could malfunction, and the trailer brakes could

213
00:07:56,402 --> 00:07:59,681
stop working, according to Motor1 and SlashGear.

214
00:08:00,031 --> 00:08:03,081
Pickup Truck and SUV Talk describes one

215
00:08:03,081 --> 00:08:05,349
part of it on the Super Duty,

216
00:08:05,349 --> 00:08:08,008
recall twenty-six V one zero four.

217
00:08:08,188 --> 00:08:11,078
A software error can make the integrated

218
00:08:11,078 --> 00:08:14,329
trailer module lose communication at startup.

219
00:08:14,509 --> 00:08:17,202
That can disable trailer brake lights and

220
00:08:17,202 --> 00:08:20,027
turn signals, and on higher-series modules,

221
00:08:20,027 --> 00:08:21,998
the trailer brakes themselves.

222
00:08:22,178 --> 00:08:25,357
Ford offered an over-the-air update or dealer

223
00:08:25,357 --> 00:08:26,346
reprogramming.

224
00:08:26,695 --> 00:08:28,007
Here is the twist.

225
00:08:28,187 --> 00:08:30,346
Ram had almost the same problem in

226
00:08:30,346 --> 00:08:31,299
the same month.

227
00:08:31,479 --> 00:08:34,510
A recall reported in early February twenty

228
00:08:34,510 --> 00:08:38,191
twenty-six covered four hundred fifty-six thousand,

229
00:08:38,191 --> 00:08:41,727
two hundred eighty-seven Ram heavy-duty vehicles,

230
00:08:41,727 --> 00:08:44,542
because a trailer tow module could make

231
00:08:44,542 --> 00:08:47,646
trailer lights fail and trailer brakes stop

232
00:08:47,646 --> 00:08:51,399
working, according to federal campaign data compiled

233
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:52,481
by Lemberg Law.

234
00:08:52,661 --> 00:08:54,922
Two rivals, two suppliers,

235
00:08:54,922 --> 00:08:56,226
one weak point.

236
00:08:56,575 --> 00:08:58,744
And this is the scary part about

237
00:08:58,744 --> 00:08:59,896
trailer problems.

238
00:09:00,076 --> 00:09:01,318
You cannot see them.

239
00:09:01,498 --> 00:09:03,106
From the driver's seat,

240
00:09:03,106 --> 00:09:04,784
everything looks normal.

241
00:09:04,964 --> 00:09:06,519
The trailer is behind you,

242
00:09:06,519 --> 00:09:08,552
the lights are behind the trailer,

243
00:09:08,552 --> 00:09:10,884
and the brakes are inside the trailer's

244
00:09:10,884 --> 00:09:11,303
wheels.

245
00:09:11,483 --> 00:09:13,397
The driver behind you is the first

246
00:09:13,397 --> 00:09:15,423
person to find out your brake lights

247
00:09:15,423 --> 00:09:15,929
are dead.

248
00:09:16,109 --> 00:09:18,262
That is why this problem deserves a

249
00:09:18,262 --> 00:09:19,430
place on this list.

250
00:09:19,779 --> 00:09:21,184
So how do you check?

251
00:09:21,364 --> 00:09:22,533
Before every trip,

252
00:09:22,533 --> 00:09:25,326
have someone stand behind the trailer while

253
00:09:25,326 --> 00:09:27,405
you press the brake and use both

254
00:09:27,405 --> 00:09:28,249
turn signals.

255
00:09:28,429 --> 00:09:31,420
Watch the trailer brake controller display on

256
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:33,680
the dash while you roll slowly and

257
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,941
apply the trailer brakes manually.

258
00:09:36,121 --> 00:09:38,017
And if you are buying a truck

259
00:09:38,017 --> 00:09:40,697
to tow, confirm the trailer module recall

260
00:09:40,697 --> 00:09:41,612
was completed.

261
00:09:41,792 --> 00:09:43,464
It is one of the cheapest safety

262
00:09:43,464 --> 00:09:44,509
checks you can make.

263
00:09:44,858 --> 00:09:47,514
Problem number four is the transmission,

264
00:09:47,514 --> 00:09:49,572
and specifically how it shifts.

265
00:09:49,752 --> 00:09:53,398
Many full-size trucks now use ten-speed automatics.

266
00:09:53,578 --> 00:09:56,403
Ford's ten R eighty was developed through

267
00:09:56,403 --> 00:09:59,160
a joint venture between Ford and General

268
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:02,192
Motors, according to Law three sixty Canada.

269
00:10:02,372 --> 00:10:05,019
More gears help fuel economy and towing.

270
00:10:05,199 --> 00:10:08,247
But owners of trucks with this transmission

271
00:10:08,247 --> 00:10:10,161
have reported harsh shifts,

272
00:10:10,161 --> 00:10:12,572
shudder and unexpected downshifts.

273
00:10:12,921 --> 00:10:15,299
In April twenty twenty-five,

274
00:10:15,299 --> 00:10:18,355
a proposed class action was filed in

275
00:10:18,355 --> 00:10:20,308
Vancouver against Ford,

276
00:10:20,308 --> 00:10:23,534
covering Canadian owners of the F-150,

277
00:10:23,534 --> 00:10:28,118
Ranger, Expedition, Mustang and Lincoln Navigator with

278
00:10:28,118 --> 00:10:29,561
the ten R eighty,

279
00:10:29,561 --> 00:10:33,297
from model years twenty seventeen and twenty

280
00:10:33,297 --> 00:10:34,655
eighteen onward.

281
00:10:34,835 --> 00:10:37,426
The suit alleges difficulty shifting,

282
00:10:37,426 --> 00:10:40,296
lunging when shifting from park to drive,

283
00:10:40,296 --> 00:10:43,376
shuddering, and sudden shifts the driver did

284
00:10:43,376 --> 00:10:44,216
not request.

285
00:10:44,396 --> 00:10:45,872
These are allegations,

286
00:10:45,872 --> 00:10:48,355
and the class has not been certified.

287
00:10:48,705 --> 00:10:49,913
Here is the twist.

288
00:10:50,093 --> 00:10:52,486
One of those complaints turned into a

289
00:10:52,486 --> 00:10:53,262
real recall.

290
00:10:53,442 --> 00:10:55,014
On April fourteenth,

291
00:10:55,014 --> 00:10:58,549
twenty twenty-six, Ford recalled one million,

292
00:10:58,549 --> 00:11:01,220
three hundred ninety-two thousand,

293
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:05,070
nine hundred thirty-five twenty fifteen to twenty

294
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:09,155
seventeen F-150s, because of an unexpected downshift

295
00:11:09,155 --> 00:11:11,747
that can cause a loss of control,

296
00:11:11,747 --> 00:11:13,319
according to Motor1.

297
00:11:13,499 --> 00:11:17,690
Federal regulators had investigated unexpected downshifts on

298
00:11:17,690 --> 00:11:19,087
these trucks before,

299
00:11:19,087 --> 00:11:21,602
according to Law three sixty Canada.

300
00:11:21,952 --> 00:11:24,587
And Ford is not alone with ten-speed

301
00:11:24,587 --> 00:11:25,319
questions.

302
00:11:25,499 --> 00:11:29,330
Consumer Reports noted transmission complaints on GM

303
00:11:29,330 --> 00:11:32,055
trucks, and Pickup Truck and SUV Talk

304
00:11:32,055 --> 00:11:35,591
reported that some twenty twenty-four and twenty

305
00:11:35,591 --> 00:11:40,010
twenty-five Silverado heavy-duty owners described valve body

306
00:11:40,010 --> 00:11:43,251
failures and full transmission replacements,

307
00:11:43,251 --> 00:11:46,713
with GM running a customer satisfaction program

308
00:11:46,713 --> 00:11:49,881
for a transmission bearing issue on certain

309
00:11:49,881 --> 00:11:51,796
twenty twenty-four trucks.

310
00:11:51,976 --> 00:11:54,779
So this is an industry-wide issue,

311
00:11:54,779 --> 00:11:56,097
not one brand's.

312
00:11:56,447 --> 00:11:57,834
How do you check on a test

313
00:11:57,834 --> 00:11:58,154
drive?

314
00:11:58,334 --> 00:11:59,692
Drive the truck cold,

315
00:11:59,692 --> 00:12:01,890
not after the dealer has warmed it

316
00:12:01,890 --> 00:12:02,084
up.

317
00:12:02,264 --> 00:12:04,651
Pay attention to the shift from park

318
00:12:04,651 --> 00:12:06,839
to drive, the first few upshifts,

319
00:12:06,839 --> 00:12:08,696
and coasting down to a stop.

320
00:12:08,876 --> 00:12:11,536
A clunk, a shudder or a delayed

321
00:12:11,536 --> 00:12:14,368
engagement is worth asking about.

322
00:12:14,548 --> 00:12:17,581
Then ask whether the transmission software has

323
00:12:17,581 --> 00:12:20,681
been updated, because many shift complaints are

324
00:12:20,681 --> 00:12:22,593
addressed with reprogramming.

325
00:12:22,773 --> 00:12:25,268
Now, problem number five could let your

326
00:12:25,268 --> 00:12:26,291
truck roll away.

327
00:12:26,641 --> 00:12:29,042
Problem number five is the rear axle,

328
00:12:29,042 --> 00:12:30,664
and it can show up in the

329
00:12:30,664 --> 00:12:32,091
worst possible moment,

330
00:12:32,091 --> 00:12:34,362
when you think the truck is parked.

331
00:12:34,542 --> 00:12:36,737
In August twenty twenty-five,

332
00:12:36,737 --> 00:12:39,536
Ford recalled up to one hundred three

333
00:12:39,536 --> 00:12:43,850
thousand, one hundred seventy-four twenty twenty-three to

334
00:12:43,850 --> 00:12:47,103
twenty twenty-five F-150s with a nine point

335
00:12:47,103 --> 00:12:49,903
seven five inch heavy-duty rear axle,

336
00:12:49,903 --> 00:12:51,644
according to RV Travel.

337
00:12:51,824 --> 00:12:54,419
The rear axle hub bolt can wear

338
00:12:54,419 --> 00:12:57,768
and snap, damaging the axle hub splines.

339
00:12:58,117 --> 00:12:59,882
And here is what that means.

340
00:13:00,062 --> 00:13:01,617
With damaged splines,

341
00:13:01,617 --> 00:13:03,987
the truck can roll away while in

342
00:13:03,987 --> 00:13:06,430
park, if the parking brake is not

343
00:13:06,430 --> 00:13:06,726
set.

344
00:13:06,906 --> 00:13:08,613
Or it can lose drive power.

345
00:13:08,793 --> 00:13:11,267
The fix is replacing both rear axle

346
00:13:11,267 --> 00:13:14,306
shafts, and owner letters were scheduled in

347
00:13:14,306 --> 00:13:17,486
phases from August twenty twenty-five all the

348
00:13:17,486 --> 00:13:19,607
way through May twenty-second,

349
00:13:19,607 --> 00:13:20,879
twenty twenty-six.

350
00:13:21,059 --> 00:13:23,823
That recall expanded an earlier one,

351
00:13:23,823 --> 00:13:26,818
numbered twenty-three V eight nine six.

352
00:13:27,167 --> 00:13:28,537
Here is the twist.

353
00:13:28,717 --> 00:13:31,655
The trucks affected are the ones built

354
00:13:31,655 --> 00:13:32,891
to tow the most,

355
00:13:32,891 --> 00:13:36,292
with the heaviest-duty rear axle Ford offers

356
00:13:36,292 --> 00:13:37,297
on the F-150.

357
00:13:37,477 --> 00:13:40,370
The option buyers choose for strength was

358
00:13:40,370 --> 00:13:42,063
the part being recalled.

359
00:13:42,243 --> 00:13:44,199
And the Super Duty had a similar

360
00:13:44,199 --> 00:13:44,565
story.

361
00:13:44,745 --> 00:13:46,436
In twenty twenty-three,

362
00:13:46,436 --> 00:13:48,862
Ford recalled forty-one thousand,

363
00:13:48,862 --> 00:13:52,979
four hundred sixty-eight twenty twenty-three F-two fifty

364
00:13:52,979 --> 00:13:56,361
and F-three fifty trucks because an incomplete

365
00:13:56,361 --> 00:13:59,154
heat treatment could let the left rear

366
00:13:59,154 --> 00:14:00,625
axle shaft fracture,

367
00:14:00,625 --> 00:14:03,198
leaving the truck unable to hold in

368
00:14:03,198 --> 00:14:06,065
park, according to Pickup Truck and SUV

369
00:14:06,065 --> 00:14:06,433
Talk.

370
00:14:06,782 --> 00:14:08,947
That makes the cheapest habit in this

371
00:14:08,947 --> 00:14:10,818
whole video also one of the most

372
00:14:10,818 --> 00:14:11,403
important.

373
00:14:11,583 --> 00:14:13,482
Always set the parking brake,

374
00:14:13,482 --> 00:14:15,577
every time, even on flat ground.

375
00:14:15,757 --> 00:14:17,832
Truck owners often skip it,

376
00:14:17,832 --> 00:14:20,215
because park feels like enough.

377
00:14:20,395 --> 00:14:23,343
These two recalls show that park depends

378
00:14:23,343 --> 00:14:26,217
on a small part inside the transmission

379
00:14:26,217 --> 00:14:28,428
and on the axle staying in one

380
00:14:28,428 --> 00:14:28,871
piece.

381
00:14:29,051 --> 00:14:31,209
The parking brake is a second,

382
00:14:31,209 --> 00:14:32,359
separate system.

383
00:14:32,539 --> 00:14:33,015
Use it.

384
00:14:33,365 --> 00:14:35,810
There is one more hidden problem that

385
00:14:35,810 --> 00:14:37,462
belongs next to the axle,

386
00:14:37,462 --> 00:14:40,105
because it also takes power away without

387
00:14:40,105 --> 00:14:40,633
warning.

388
00:14:40,813 --> 00:14:42,379
In twenty twenty-five,

389
00:14:42,379 --> 00:14:45,795
Ford recalled about eight hundred fifty thousand

390
00:14:45,795 --> 00:14:47,645
Ford and Lincoln vehicles,

391
00:14:47,645 --> 00:14:51,132
including more than one hundred thirteen thousand

392
00:14:51,132 --> 00:14:53,694
Super Duty trucks with the six point

393
00:14:53,694 --> 00:14:56,256
two, six point eight and seven point

394
00:14:56,256 --> 00:14:57,964
three liter gas engines,

395
00:14:57,964 --> 00:15:01,166
because the low-pressure fuel pump could lose

396
00:15:01,166 --> 00:15:03,301
pressure and stall the engine,

397
00:15:03,301 --> 00:15:06,077
according to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk.

398
00:15:06,426 --> 00:15:08,591
And here is the detail that makes

399
00:15:08,591 --> 00:15:10,560
it a nobody-warns-you problem.

400
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:13,425
The report says failure is more likely

401
00:15:13,425 --> 00:15:15,685
with low fuel or in hot weather.

402
00:15:15,865 --> 00:15:18,141
That is exactly the situation of a

403
00:15:18,141 --> 00:15:19,815
work truck in the summer,

404
00:15:19,815 --> 00:15:22,091
running on the last quarter of the

405
00:15:22,091 --> 00:15:23,296
tank between jobs.

406
00:15:23,476 --> 00:15:26,597
Ford says the affected trucks were built

407
00:15:26,597 --> 00:15:29,874
from July twenty twenty-one to July twenty

408
00:15:29,874 --> 00:15:30,732
twenty-two.

409
00:15:30,912 --> 00:15:33,490
The Power Stroke diesels were not included.

410
00:15:33,839 --> 00:15:36,521
Problem number six has the scariest name.

411
00:15:36,701 --> 00:15:39,012
Owners call it the death wobble.

412
00:15:39,192 --> 00:15:41,135
It is a violent shaking of the

413
00:15:41,135 --> 00:15:43,597
front end that can start after hitting

414
00:15:43,597 --> 00:15:45,152
a bump at highway speed,

415
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:47,679
according to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk.

416
00:15:47,859 --> 00:15:50,575
It is most associated with solid front

417
00:15:50,575 --> 00:15:53,292
axle trucks, like the Ford Super Duty.

418
00:15:53,472 --> 00:15:54,881
And when it happens,

419
00:15:54,881 --> 00:15:57,557
the steering wheel shakes so hard that

420
00:15:57,557 --> 00:16:00,163
many drivers have to slow down almost

421
00:16:00,163 --> 00:16:01,924
to a stop before it ends.

422
00:16:02,275 --> 00:16:03,795
Here is what is documented.

423
00:16:03,975 --> 00:16:06,539
Pickup Truck and SUV Talk reports that

424
00:16:06,539 --> 00:16:08,630
Ford redesigned the suspension,

425
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:10,991
that the redesign did not fully fix

426
00:16:10,991 --> 00:16:13,756
the problem, and that reports now suggest

427
00:16:13,756 --> 00:16:16,050
it is far less common than before.

428
00:16:16,230 --> 00:16:19,481
Owners typically fix it by replacing track

429
00:16:19,481 --> 00:16:22,499
bars, ball joints and steering dampers.

430
00:16:22,679 --> 00:16:24,991
And no recall has been issued for

431
00:16:24,991 --> 00:16:28,004
this issue on twenty twenty-three to twenty

432
00:16:28,004 --> 00:16:30,667
twenty-six F-Series Super Duty trucks.

433
00:16:31,017 --> 00:16:32,886
And here is the twist in court.

434
00:16:33,066 --> 00:16:35,642
A class action over death wobble on

435
00:16:35,642 --> 00:16:38,586
older Super Duty trucks has been running

436
00:16:38,586 --> 00:16:40,206
for about seven years.

437
00:16:40,386 --> 00:16:41,936
In twenty twenty-six,

438
00:16:41,936 --> 00:16:43,560
according to Autoblog,

439
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:45,332
a federal appeals court,

440
00:16:45,332 --> 00:16:46,661
the Ninth Circuit,

441
00:16:46,661 --> 00:16:49,983
reversed the class certification and sent the

442
00:16:49,983 --> 00:16:52,124
case back to the lower court.

443
00:16:52,304 --> 00:16:55,100
It accepted Ford's argument that the problem

444
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:57,706
showed up at different rates across years

445
00:16:57,706 --> 00:16:58,596
and platforms.

446
00:16:58,776 --> 00:17:00,248
The case is not over,

447
00:17:00,248 --> 00:17:02,422
but it looks weaker for owners.

448
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:04,802
So if you are buying a used

449
00:17:04,802 --> 00:17:07,885
heavy-duty truck with a solid front axle,

450
00:17:07,885 --> 00:17:09,689
drive it on the highway,

451
00:17:09,689 --> 00:17:12,246
and over a few expansion joints or

452
00:17:12,246 --> 00:17:13,975
rough patches at speed.

453
00:17:14,155 --> 00:17:16,044
Ask whether the track bar,

454
00:17:16,044 --> 00:17:18,951
ball joints or steering damper have been

455
00:17:18,951 --> 00:17:20,332
replaced, and when.

456
00:17:20,512 --> 00:17:23,305
And be careful with oversized tires and

457
00:17:23,305 --> 00:17:26,886
lifts, because they change the front-end geometry.

458
00:17:27,066 --> 00:17:29,261
A front end that has been maintained

459
00:17:29,261 --> 00:17:31,335
is a very different truck from one

460
00:17:31,335 --> 00:17:32,127
that has not.

461
00:17:32,478 --> 00:17:35,682
Notice something about problems five and six.

462
00:17:35,862 --> 00:17:37,978
Both are made worse by how trucks

463
00:17:37,978 --> 00:17:38,555
are used.

464
00:17:38,735 --> 00:17:41,342
Towing, hauling, lifting,

465
00:17:41,342 --> 00:17:43,428
big tires, hot days,

466
00:17:43,428 --> 00:17:44,366
low fuel.

467
00:17:44,546 --> 00:17:46,578
The trucks most likely to show these

468
00:17:46,578 --> 00:17:48,553
problems are the ones that work the

469
00:17:48,553 --> 00:17:49,004
hardest.

470
00:17:49,184 --> 00:17:51,168
So if a used truck spent its

471
00:17:51,168 --> 00:17:53,576
life towing or carries a lift kit,

472
00:17:53,576 --> 00:17:56,338
the checks we just covered matter twice

473
00:17:56,338 --> 00:17:56,905
as much.

474
00:17:57,255 --> 00:17:58,361
Before we finish,

475
00:17:58,361 --> 00:18:00,445
a bonus problem that is rare but

476
00:18:00,445 --> 00:18:02,919
expensive, and that is exactly why you

477
00:18:02,919 --> 00:18:03,895
should know it.

478
00:18:04,075 --> 00:18:07,472
The General Motors three liter Duramax diesel,

479
00:18:07,472 --> 00:18:08,431
the L Z zero,

480
00:18:08,431 --> 00:18:11,680
in the Silverado and Sierra fifteen hundred.

481
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:14,829
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk,

482
00:18:14,829 --> 00:18:17,721
a small number of owners have reported

483
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:20,994
failures of the crankshaft thrust bearings,

484
00:18:20,994 --> 00:18:24,496
which can cause excessive crankshaft end play,

485
00:18:24,496 --> 00:18:25,790
low oil pressure,

486
00:18:25,790 --> 00:18:28,454
and in some cases a complete engine

487
00:18:28,454 --> 00:18:29,368
replacement.

488
00:18:29,718 --> 00:18:31,674
In June twenty twenty-six,

489
00:18:31,674 --> 00:18:34,383
a teardown of one failed engine with

490
00:18:34,383 --> 00:18:37,770
about seven thousand five hundred miles found

491
00:18:37,770 --> 00:18:40,253
only one complete thrust bearing,

492
00:18:40,253 --> 00:18:42,210
plus fragments of another.

493
00:18:42,390 --> 00:18:44,865
The writer suggested the engine may have

494
00:18:44,865 --> 00:18:47,341
left the factory with a bearing missing,

495
00:18:47,341 --> 00:18:49,321
but noted that cannot be proven.

496
00:18:49,501 --> 00:18:52,625
The report stresses that failures are relatively

497
00:18:52,625 --> 00:18:55,489
uncommon among the thousands of these trucks

498
00:18:55,489 --> 00:18:56,270
on the road.

499
00:18:56,450 --> 00:18:58,574
Rare, but worth asking about.

500
00:18:58,924 --> 00:19:01,177
And one more quiet problem from Ram.

501
00:19:01,357 --> 00:19:03,655
In September twenty twenty-four,

502
00:19:03,655 --> 00:19:05,954
Stellantis recalled one million,

503
00:19:05,954 --> 00:19:08,396
two hundred twenty-seven thousand,

504
00:19:08,396 --> 00:19:11,484
eight hundred eight Ram fifteen hundreds in

505
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:12,777
the United States,

506
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:16,297
because the anti-lock brake module software could

507
00:19:16,297 --> 00:19:18,954
disable electronic stability control,

508
00:19:18,954 --> 00:19:20,606
according to CarScoops.

509
00:19:20,786 --> 00:19:22,980
The brakes still worked normally.

510
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,432
But a safety system that helps prevent

511
00:19:25,432 --> 00:19:27,883
skids could switch off without the driver

512
00:19:27,883 --> 00:19:28,362
knowing.

513
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,713
A software update fixed it.

514
00:19:31,062 --> 00:19:33,533
Put those two together and you see

515
00:19:33,533 --> 00:19:36,294
why software matters even for the most

516
00:19:36,294 --> 00:19:37,819
basic safety systems.

517
00:19:37,999 --> 00:19:38,919
In one case,

518
00:19:38,919 --> 00:19:41,833
a stability system could be turned off

519
00:19:41,833 --> 00:19:42,446
by code.

520
00:19:42,626 --> 00:19:45,308
In another, trailer brakes could be turned

521
00:19:45,308 --> 00:19:46,074
off by code.

522
00:19:46,254 --> 00:19:48,058
Neither one would show up on a

523
00:19:48,058 --> 00:19:49,080
quick test drive,

524
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,823
and neither one shows up as a

525
00:19:50,823 --> 00:19:52,686
warning light you would notice.

526
00:19:52,866 --> 00:19:54,556
The only way to know is the

527
00:19:54,556 --> 00:19:55,432
recall record.

528
00:19:55,781 --> 00:19:58,243
So look at the six problems together.

529
00:19:58,423 --> 00:20:00,188
A screen that freezes.

530
00:20:00,368 --> 00:20:02,155
A camera that goes black.

531
00:20:02,335 --> 00:20:04,855
A trailer module that drops out.

532
00:20:05,035 --> 00:20:07,450
A transmission that shifts on its own.

533
00:20:07,630 --> 00:20:10,082
An axle that lets the truck roll

534
00:20:10,082 --> 00:20:10,695
in park.

535
00:20:10,875 --> 00:20:12,632
And a front end that shakes at

536
00:20:12,632 --> 00:20:13,452
highway speed.

537
00:20:13,632 --> 00:20:15,340
Only two of them are the kind

538
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:18,578
of mechanical problem your grandfather would recognize.

539
00:20:18,758 --> 00:20:21,370
The rest are electronics and software.

540
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,694
And here is the final twist.

541
00:20:23,874 --> 00:20:27,531
The electronic problems are the most common,

542
00:20:27,531 --> 00:20:29,941
but often the easiest to fix,

543
00:20:29,941 --> 00:20:32,767
a software update at the dealer or

544
00:20:32,767 --> 00:20:33,847
over the air.

545
00:20:34,027 --> 00:20:35,826
The mechanical ones are rarer,

546
00:20:35,826 --> 00:20:37,625
but they are the ones that can

547
00:20:37,625 --> 00:20:39,484
cost you, or put you in danger.

548
00:20:39,664 --> 00:20:42,288
So a smart buyer tests both.

549
00:20:42,468 --> 00:20:44,474
You play with the screen and the

550
00:20:44,474 --> 00:20:45,602
camera like a kid,

551
00:20:45,602 --> 00:20:47,421
and you drive the truck cold,

552
00:20:47,421 --> 00:20:48,361
on the highway,

553
00:20:48,361 --> 00:20:49,364
like a mechanic.

554
00:20:49,714 --> 00:20:52,163
Here is the checklist for twenty twenty-seven.

555
00:20:52,343 --> 00:20:54,851
One, connect your phone and test the

556
00:20:54,851 --> 00:20:55,339
screen.

557
00:20:55,519 --> 00:20:58,428
Two, reverse five times and watch the

558
00:20:58,428 --> 00:20:58,978
camera.

559
00:20:59,158 --> 00:21:01,747
Three, test trailer lights with a helper.

560
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:05,399
Four, drive cold and feel every shift.

561
00:21:05,579 --> 00:21:08,028
Five, check that the parking brake holds

562
00:21:08,028 --> 00:21:08,702
on a slope.

563
00:21:08,882 --> 00:21:11,698
Six, test the steering at highway speed

